The space Policy Options worth setting Up to a few hundred points <code>sweep</code> (the default) <code>batch_size</code> Large, and better neighbours are found step by step <code>gradient</code> <code>steps</code>, <code>wave</code>, <code>patience</code>, <code>reach</code> Large and rugged <code>anneal</code> <code>steps</code>, <code>temperature</code>, <code>cooling</code>, <code>seed</code> Large, and good settings combine <code>genetic</code> <code>population</code>, <code>generations</code>, <code>mutation</code> Just a feel for the space <code>montecarlo</code> <code>samples</code>, <code>seed</code> Two objectives traded against each other <code>pareto</code> <code>budget</code>, <code>reference</code>, <code>scale</code> FluxAgent proposing points from what was measured <code>flux</code> <code>rounds</code>, <code>batch_size</code>, <code>shown</code> <p>Phases run in order, each from where the last ended:</p> <pre><code>flow:
  orchestrate:
    space: {block: [16, 32, 64, 128], order: [ijk, ikj, jki]}
    policy:
      - {name: coarse, policy: sweep, knobs: [block]}
      - {name: fine, policy: gradient, hold: [block], steps: 20}
</code></pre> <p>Every option is in Search policies.</p>
